{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CetGxkKrj18jsNKBvs6gg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n```\n\n**Proposed changes:**\n\n**1. ApiError.kt** — Add `SHIPMENT_CANNOT_CONFIRM` error code to the `ErrorCode` enum. This will be thrown when attempting to confirm a shipment that is already in CANCELLED status.\n\n**2. ShipmentController.kt** — Add a new `@PostMapping(\"/{shipmentId}/confirm\")` method that:\n   - Retrieves the shipment by ID using the repository\n   - Throws `ResourceNotFoundException` if not found (404)\n   - If status is CANCELLED, throws `ConflictException` with SHIPMENT_CANNOT_CONFIRM code (409)\n   - If status is CREATED, updates it to CONFIRMED and saves\n   - If status is CONFIRMED, does nothing (idempotent - already confirmed)\n   - Returns the updated (or unchanged) shipment with 200 status\n\n**3. ShipmentControllerTest.kt** — Add four new test cases:\n   - `confirms a created shipment and transitions to CONFIRMED`\n   - `idempotently handles confirming an already CONFIRMED shipment`\n   - `rejects confirming a CANCELLED shipment with 409 and error code`\n   - `rejects confirming a non-existent shipment with 404 and error code`\n\n**Alternative considered and rejected:**\n- Adding a service layer between controller and repository: This would be over-engineering for an in-memory repository and a simple state transition. The controller can directly handle the logic here, consistent with the existing Create endpoint which also does validation and state management directly in the controller.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n1. **Confirm CREATED shipment** → repository.findById() → check status is CREATED → update status to CONFIRMED → repository.save() → return 200 with updated Shipment\n2. **Confirm already CONFIRMED** → repository.findById() → check status is CONFIRMED → return 200 with unchanged Shipment (idempotent)\n3. **Confirm CANCELLED** → repository.findById() → check status is CANCELLED → throw ConflictException(SHIPMENT_CANNOT_CONFIRM) → GlobalExceptionHandler catches it → return 409 with error envelope\n4. **Confirm non-existent** → repository.findById() returns null → throw ResourceNotFoundException(SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND) → GlobalExceptionHandler catches it → return 404 with error envelope\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\n1. Test confirming CREATED shipment: Create S-1, confirm it, verify status is CONFIRMED, verify returns 200\n2. Test idempotent confirm: Create S-2, confirm once, confirm again, verify both succeed and status is still CONFIRMED\n3. Test cancelling CANCELLED: Insert a CANCELLED shipment directly into repository (like the fixture comment suggests), attempt confirm, verify 409 with SHIPMENT_CANNOT_CONFIRM code\n4. Test non-existent: Attempt confirm on S-missing, verify 404 with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND code\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n```\n\nNow I'll implement the changes:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2146,"cache_read_input_tokens":19174,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2146},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6483e458-b4d0-4b1e-a39f-335763f04229","uuid":"54d66ca2-70ef-4594-9ea3-af810d22a5cc","timestamp":"2026-09-09T17:40:47.947Z","request_id":"req_011CetGxjheYxMEqYufZicWD"}
